{"author":{"id":"8022379585b4ab99ca8775db3eb67d33fcb256817114c28e51ccc1e9f55cdec4"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1790998636,"nonce":"2O/R7g3meFCPtF7ovEZw5XNoxBs=","title":"Methods taken as values where only the call form resolved","message":"`recv.m` not followed by a call became a placeholder field (E0100, or a call of a zero-argument method on the spot) whenever TAST found no method symbol for it, although `recv.m(..)` resolved. It now lowers to `{ var r = recv; function(a, ..) return r.m(a, ..); }` for:\n\n- a method of a builtin Array or String, typed from its declaration in Array.hx/String.hx with the class `T` bound to the element type; a trailing optional parameter left null is dropped from the call so the method's default applies (Issue1997, Issue5078);\n- a static extension in scope, including one from a `using` of a class declared later in the same file, which was never registered (usings are lowered before the file's classes);\n- a method an abstract forwards to its underlying class (Issue8200).\n\nAlso:\n- `var s = C; s.staticMethod` bound the class value as an argument; it is `C.staticMethod` (Issue3030).\n- `e.A` on a value of an enum type is the constructor (Issue6159).\n- A field read on a type-parameter receiver goes by name instead of failing the compile (Issue9593).\n- `Array.push` returned nothing: `var n = a.push(x)` vanished or read garbage. It returns the new length (Issue10754 via `a.push.bind()`).\n\nGate: 806 -\u003e 813, 0 lost, 0 moved; suite 206/0/2; fixtures, compiler integration tests, clippy clean.\n\nNot fixed here: Issue2497 (extension held in a static var; comment on 976a7d1), Issue4327/Issue5009 (@:callable), Issue6007 (structural iteration over a function field; comment on 694ff71), Issue6705 (function identity, 069ce9d).","files":null}]}